; A P directive whose parenthesized price evaluates to several commodities
; (a basket, see 1101.test) gives the commodity a value expression rebuilt
; from that balance's components.  The components must keep their full
; precision: Ledger used to print them at their commodity's display
; precision, so EUR 1/4 (EUR shows no decimals here) was stored as EUR 0,
; and GBP 0.12345 under `format GBP 1.00` as GBP 0.12, and every later -X
; valuation of the basket was wrong.  EUR 1/3 keeps the six extra digits
; that division gives (EUR 0.333333), as any amount in Ledger does.
;
; The rebuilt text is read without learning display styles from it, so
; the full-precision components do not widen how EUR is shown elsewhere:
; Assets:Cash still shows EUR 1.

commodity GBP
    format GBP 1.00

P 2015-01-01 EUR $1.00
P 2015-01-01 GBP $1.00
P 2015-01-01 bicur (EUR 1/4 + $0.55)
P 2015-01-01 tricur (EUR 1/3 + $0.55)
P 2015-01-01 fmtcur (GBP 0.12345 + $0.55)

2015/01/01 Baskets
    Assets:Bicur       3000 bicur
    Assets:Fmtcur      3000 fmtcur
    Assets:Tricur      3000 tricur
    Equity

2015/01/01 Euros
    Assets:Cash        EUR 1
    Equity

test bal Assets:Bicur Assets:Fmtcur Assets:Tricur -X $ --now 2015/02/01
            $7070.35  Assets
            $2400.00    Bicur
            $2020.35    Fmtcur
            $2650.00    Tricur
--------------------
            $7070.35
end test

test bal Assets:Cash
               EUR 1  Assets:Cash
end test

test print Bicur
2015/01/01 Baskets
    Assets:Bicur                        3000 bicur ((({$0.55} + {EUR 0.25})))
    Assets:Fmtcur                       3000 fmtcur ((({$0.55} + {GBP 0.12345})))
    Assets:Tricur                       3000 tricur ((({$0.55} + {EUR 0.333333})))
    Equity
end test
